Many stop off to camp and fish at remote camping grounds along the rivers and highways. Great gorges and ice cold fresh waterholes flowing to vast river systems that fork across the top end and further west into the Kimberley region. This is in stark contrast to the arid dry red desert of the southern part of the Northern Territory known as the Red Centre. If you travel west from the top end and cross over the border into western Australia on the one and only road that you can travel, you instantly hit the Kimberley region. The Kimberley is the northernmost region of western Australia, covering Australia's entire

