00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:38.000
That's a popular drawcard for people who want to get off the beaten track and experience the rugged dramatic landscape of the Australian Outback. In contrast to the steep terrain in the north, the southern end of the Kimberley is flatter with a dry tropical grassland. It's home to over 30 large cattle stations. Camping, fishing, swimming, bushwalking, scenic flights, charter boat tours, four-wheel driving, and indigenous history experiences are all popular activities for tourists and locals in the Kimberley.

7
00:03:38.000 --> 00:04:15.000
