No one knew who was responsible, whether it was more than one person, or if it was going to happen again. In the western Australian Kimberley region, approximately 37km from the Northern Territory border is the town of Kananara. It has located 226km west of Timber Creek, where the Bullens were murdered. If you're driving across the top end from Timber Creek through the Kimberley region across the Broome, there is only one route. That route is along the Victoria Highway, which takes you through Kananara.

