where you can escape and get away from it all. But like the Victoria River, the Pentecost is also home to a large saltwater crocodile population, so you need to be careful. Julie, Philip, and Terry set up camp at the picnic area, and they were soon joined by their two other friends, David McKenzie and Daniel Rowe, who drove in a separate car. The group fished into the night, going to bed around midnight. They ate breakfast together the next morning, June 14th, before their two friends David McKenzie and Daniel Rowe left and returned to Kananara.

